{
    "word": "gigantomachy",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e7614b5e-3894-3e63-a50e-f76ca63c015b",
                "word": "gigantomachy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "14c72310-71a9-4aad-a40c-0f6edf7d3026",
                        "entry_id": "e7614b5e-3894-3e63-a50e-f76ca63c015b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "gigantomachies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef6f7b33-35b8-389e-a8b8-83193d41bfa9",
                        "entry_id": "e7614b5e-3894-3e63-a50e-f76ca63c015b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The battle of the Giants (offspring of Gaia, according to Hesiod conceived from the spilt blood of Uranus) against the Olympian gods."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Greek",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6220528-1e45-4de3-9061-cb52160e7a42",
                                "sense_id": "ef6f7b33-35b8-389e-a8b8-83193d41bfa9",
                                "text": "Here we will examine Amazonomachies, Gigantomachies, and Centauromachies; the Trojan War will be discussed in Chapter 7."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20a49045-2e28-40c3-a94c-bf55c2350333",
                                "sense_id": "ef6f7b33-35b8-389e-a8b8-83193d41bfa9",
                                "text": "You often see the Gigantomachy in the sculptural decoration of Archaic temples: the statement of the authority of the gods, made by the temple itself, is reinforced by the myth told upon it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46e89dc0-ee52-4ff1-8ef7-d5d72be84b9b",
                                "sense_id": "ef6f7b33-35b8-389e-a8b8-83193d41bfa9",
                                "text": "First, beginning in the 5th cent. BC, the line between religious and commemorative-political art became blurred as traditional subjects were blurred to convey political meanings (e.g. the Amazonomachy, the Gigantomachy; see AMAZONS, GIANTS)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "350b31bf-cd72-32e6-adc8-6b589b66c1f2",
                        "entry_id": "e7614b5e-3894-3e63-a50e-f76ca63c015b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any battle envisaged as being waged by giants against gods or against an established universal order."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3de694a3-7346-4b10-ba0c-a450595865d0",
                                "sense_id": "350b31bf-cd72-32e6-adc8-6b589b66c1f2",
                                "text": "Giant and dragon interchange as opponents of god or hero in folklore; in the gigantomachies we have evidence of their near-identity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3512be0-9189-4588-b4b6-1de88475d926",
                                "sense_id": "350b31bf-cd72-32e6-adc8-6b589b66c1f2",
                                "text": "Beginning with the presentation of the giants in c.m. 53, supported by the Greek Gigantomachia and the recurring giant theme from the De Raptu Proserpinae, it is then possible to analyse the construction of the Visigothic leader Alaric to demonstrate the way in which he, in particular, is depicted as a monster figure and his assault on Roman land as a new gigantomachy.[…]To write a gigantomachy is to engage with a long tradition associated with the theme."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "273fa06e-c0bb-44ea-b359-952abd4e3bed",
                        "source_entry_id": "e7614b5e-3894-3e63-a50e-f76ca63c015b",
                        "source_sense_description": "uprising of the Giants against the Olympian gods",
                        "target_lang_word": "gigantomachie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gigantomachie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bdf0d789-1827-3fab-8439-0b580af08e59",
                                        "entry_id": "1637d5fc-a6ee-30aa-81de-dc2e9f405b85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Combat de géants contre les dieux."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Mythologie grecque"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18eae6f4-1415-4ba8-ac0c-f33aa2aa41dc",
                                                "sense_id": "bdf0d789-1827-3fab-8439-0b580af08e59",
                                                "text": "Des bourrasques répétées avec force balaient la campagne ; c’est le dieu Thor, fils d’Odin, armé de son marteau, qui écrase les crânes de ses ennemis. Sa barbe est rousse, sa force sans limites, il est l’ennemi des géants, monstres effroyables au corps terminé en serpent. On entend des frappements sourds. Broûmm ! Broûmm ! Puissant, rusé, Thor veut s’affirmer ; il est le plus fort et ce sont des gigantomachies. Les mauvais subissent le pire : la métamorphose instantané en pierre. Et ce sont des trolls, des elfes, des femmes statufiées témoignant de cette vie des antres des montagnes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "83daffcf-0ac4-3bdf-82d8-771a227d2ebd",
                                        "entry_id": "1637d5fc-a6ee-30aa-81de-dc2e9f405b85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Représentation artistique de ce combat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65539b10-897c-47b8-ba35-4cf850954e64",
                                                "sense_id": "83daffcf-0ac4-3bdf-82d8-771a227d2ebd",
                                                "text": "Bien que la plupart des cas cités ne puissent être datés ni précisément ni définitivement, il semble que les sculptures de Sens soient les premières à illustrer dans la pierre le thème de la gigantomachie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45cff9fa-0fdf-4962-a6dd-be5bb0b05ac6",
                                                "sense_id": "83daffcf-0ac4-3bdf-82d8-771a227d2ebd",
                                                "text": "La ville morte était devenue une jungle pavée, un jardin suspendu de troncs sauvages, une gigantomachie déchaînée de l'arbre et de la pierre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbd709ea-ee80-30fc-9077-ecaee6855e4d",
                                        "entry_id": "1637d5fc-a6ee-30aa-81de-dc2e9f405b85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Évocation de ce combat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0634b40-1285-43ef-96a6-d0665a82edfc",
                                                "sense_id": "fbd709ea-ee80-30fc-9077-ecaee6855e4d",
                                                "text": "Et lentement, avec les siècles, la ville morte était devenue une jungle pavée, un jardin suspendu de troncs sauvages, une gigantomachie déchaînée de l’arbre et de la pierre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
